diagnostic_evidence.quote:
For \(s>1/2\), the Sobolev embedding \(H^s(I) \hookrightarrow C^{0,s-1/2}(\overline I)\) yields
\begin{equation}
|v(x)-v(y)| \le C |x-y|^{s-1/2} \|v\|_{H^s(I)}
\qquad
\forall x,y \in \overline I
\label{eq:holder-embed-1d}
\end{equation}

Using the boundedness of restriction to normal fibers in tubular coordinates, together with the equivalence of Sobolev norms under smooth coordinate transformations, we have
\begin{equation}
\int_{\partial \Omega} \|w_y\|_{H^s(-\delta,\delta)}^2 \, d\sigma(y)
\lesssim
\|v\|_{H^s(U_\delta(\partial \Omega))}^2
\label{eq:normal-fiber-bound-hd}
\end{equation}

Using standard estimates for multiplication and composition, we get
\begin{equation}
\|u_*^e\|_{H^{s}(\IR^d)}
\lesssim
\|u^e\circ q_\delta\|_{H^{s}(U_{\delta_2}(\partial\Omega_\delta))}
\lesssim
\|u^e\|_{H^{s}( U_{\delta_2}(\partial\Omega_\delta))}
\label{eq:u-star-hp1-bound}
\end{equation}

Since \(\partial\Omega_\delta\) is assumed smooth, the dual solution \(\phi\) satisfies the elliptic regularity estimate
\begin{equation}
\|\phi\|_{H^2(\Omega_\delta)} \lesssim \|e_h\|_{\Omega_\delta}
\label{eq:l2-dual-regularity}
\end{equation}

let \(\phi \in H^1_0(\Omega_\delta)\) solve the dual problem
\begin{equation}
-\Delta \phi = e_h
\qquad \text{in } \Omega_\delta
\label{eq:l2-dual}
\end{equation}

